IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`

-- Cat Regulations 2012 — SCHEDULE 3, FEES (cl 1), payable under reg 11(1)(b)
-- (registration, s 8(2)(b)) and reg 21(b) (approval to breed, s 36(2)(b)).
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-regulations-2012.txt lines 698-729.
--
-- Amounts are Australian dollars. The figure computed is the fee payable
-- under cl 1(2) and (3). cl 1(4) — "A local government may reduce or waive
-- a fee payable under subclause (2) or (3) in respect of any individual cat
-- or any class of cats within its district" — is a discretion this encoding
-- does not exercise: the figure is the most that can be charged, and a
-- local government's reduction or waiver is a further fact about the case.

§ `Schedule 3 — Fees`

§§ `1. Fees payable`

§§§ `The Table`

-- Item 1: "Fee for application for grant or renewal of the registration of
-- a cat for one year — (a) if application is for grant of registration and
-- is made after 31 May for registration until the next 31 October ... $10.00
-- (b) otherwise ... $20.00".
--
-- FORK F-10: "after 31 May" is read as after 31 May and no later than the
-- 31 October that ends the same registration year (reg 12(2): registration
-- years run to 31 October), i.e. an application made in June to October. An
-- application on 15 December is "after 31 May" on the calendar but the
-- registration it buys runs for more than ten months, which is the case
-- item 1(a) exists to discount.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1, Table item 1(a)
GIVEN g IS A `Grant or renewal`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `item 1(a) applies to` g `made on` d IF
        g EQUALS `a grant`
    AND d GREATER THAN YMD (DATE_YEAR d) 5 31
    AND d AT MOST     YMD (DATE_YEAR d) 10 31

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1(2), Table items 1-3
GIVEN app IS A `Registration application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table fee for` app MEANS
    IF   NOT `the law is encoded for` (app's `date made`)
    THEN REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"
    ELSE CONSIDER app's `term applied for`
         WHEN `one year`            THEN IF   `item 1(a) applies to` (app's `grant or renewal`) `made on` (app's `date made`)
                                         THEN 10.00                                                 -- item 1(a)
                                         ELSE 20.00                                                 -- item 1(b)
         WHEN `3 years`             THEN 42.50                                                      -- item 2
         WHEN `the life of the cat` THEN 100.00                                                     -- item 3

-- Item 4: "Fee for application for grant or renewal of approval to breed
-- cats ... $100.00 per breeding cat (male or female)".
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1(2), Table item 4
GIVEN app IS A `Breeding application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table fee for the breeding application` app MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for` (app's `date made`)
    THEN 100.00 TIMES app's `number of breeding cats`
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"

§§§ `Pensioners`

-- cl 1(1): "pensioner means an eligible pensioner as defined in the Rates and
-- Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 section 3(1)" — an input.
-- cl 1(3): "Despite subclause (2), if the owner of a cat is a pensioner, the
-- fee payable for an application for the grant or renewal of the
-- registration of the cat is 50% of the fee that would otherwise be payable
-- under subclause (2)." It does not reach item 4.
--
-- FORK F-11: cl 1(3) turns on "the owner of a cat", not on the applicant.
-- Only an owner may apply (s 8(1)), so the applicant is read as the owner
-- whose pensioner status counts.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1(1), (3)
GIVEN app IS A `Registration application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the registration fee payable for` app MEANS
    IF   app's `applicant`'s `an eligible pensioner`
    THEN `the Table fee for` app TIMES 50%
    ELSE `the Table fee for` app

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1(2); reg 21(b)
GIVEN app IS A `Breeding application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the breeding approval fee payable for` app MEANS
    `the Table fee for the breeding application` app
